According to some sources in other forums, it seems that a device kernel can call `thrust::sort` under the following conditions:

1. It serializes the execution to that single kernel, by setting `thrust::seq` as policy → No parallel gains in our case
2. It spawns further kernels via dynamic parallelism, by setting `thrust::device` as policy → Parallel gains, but dynamic parallelism is involved.
  
